WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:04.170
- Over 2,000 years ago,
the city of Zhenyuan

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.450
was built on a natural moat.

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.930
Sandwiched between mountains,

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.200
intending to keep intruders out.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.830
But today, tourists
flow through the streets

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.183
of the famous Venice of the Orient.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:24.800
Built in 205 BC during the Qin Dynasty,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.760
The Wuyang River divides
the city into two parts:

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:31.240
East and West.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.400
Numerous small canals, rivers and bridges

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.533
dot the landscape of this ancient city.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.060
The city also thrived from trade.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:42.220
The Silk Road of the South
went through this city

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.830
because it was the only
access point by ship

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.770
from South China to the central plains.

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:49.160
Merchant ships were docked here

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.760
from Vietnam, Thailand and India,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.840
eager to move through
the port to the capital.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.490
Today, you will find
remnants of old and new

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:00.260
married perfectly in this ancient city.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.660
As day turns to night,

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:05.080
the stunning views turn
into a neon wonderland.

